lity":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":null,"_score_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":1.2758687785456635,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":100.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.1410193387552043,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.017662655959555077,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":22.6,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.15828275505662082,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":86.1,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.010361157730533014,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":22.6,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004848810931965497,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.08728,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":58.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Concentra Group Holdings Parent, Inc. provides occupational health services in the United States. The company operates in three segments: Occupational Health centers, Onsite health clinics, and Other business. It offers occupational health services, including workers compensation, employer, and consumer health services; and employer-sponsored primary care services at workplace, including mobile health and episodic specialty testing services. It also operates Concentra Telemed, a telemedicine platform for the treatment of work-related injuries and illnesses; Concentra Pharmacy for distributing repackaged medications; and Concentra Medical Compliance Administration, a third-party administrator that helps to manage abuse testing programs for employers with regulated or non-regulated workforces. In addition, the company provides injury care, primary care, urgent care, preventive care, clinical testing, physical examinations and evaluations, drug and alcohol screenings, clinical testing, vaccinations and other preventive care, and a range of consultative services designed to protect employees from workplace hazards. The company was founded in 1979 and is based in Addison, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew T. DiCanio M.B.A. | President, CEO & Director | Age 42 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $217K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $20K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Concentra Group Holdings Parent is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $5.3B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 136% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 128-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $197M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.68\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 8.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Goodwill represents 52% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.36964496179465983},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $13.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 25% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months